{"indicator":"pedestrians","unit":"%","years":[2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021],"latestWithin":5,"notes":{"TWN":"台灣用交通部的 30 日內死亡人數（每年都有）：行人死亡 2022 年 394 人、2025 年 354 人（占 12.4%）。2022 年 12 月 CNN 的旅遊專欄引用網友的說法，形容台灣是「行人地獄」（a living hell for pedestrians），這個說法之後在國內廣泛流傳，也帶動民間對行人安全的訴求。交通部 2023 年 8 月向行政院提出「行人交通安全政策綱領」（2024–2027 年），《道路交通安全基本法》2023 年 12 月公布、2024 年 1 月 1 日施行，以 2050 年道路交通事故零死亡為目標。"},"notesEn":{"TWN":"Taiwan uses Ministry of Transportation and Communications deaths within 30 days (every year): 394 pedestrians died in 2022 and 354 in 2025 (12.4% of road deaths). In December 2022 a CNN travel column quoted a description of Taiwan as \"a living hell for pedestrians\"; the phrase spread widely in Taiwan and fed public calls for safer streets. The Ministry presented a pedestrian traffic safety policy framework (2024–2027) to the Executive Yuan in August 2023, and the Road Traffic Safety Basic Act, promulgated in December 2023 and in force from 1 January 2024, sets a goal of zero road deaths by 2050."},"encoding":"delta","values":{"ERI":[-1,254,null,null,null,null,-4],"EGY":[-1,269,null,null,null,null,-19],"COM":[-1,174,null,null,null,null,87],"FIN":[-1,107,null,null,null,null,3],"GHA":[-1,461,null,null,null,-149,null],"GRC":[-1,181,null,null,null,-51,null],"FRA":[-1,161,null,null,null,null,-20],"FSM":[0,50,null,null,null,null,null],"GEO":[-1,265,null,null,null,null,0],"HUN":[0,25,null,null,null,null,0],"HND":[-1,279,null,null,null,null,58],"HRV":[-1,218,null,null,null,null,-91],"GTM":[-1,392,null,null,null,null,-92],"GUY":[-1,297,null,null,null,null,-14],"ISL":[-1,111,null,null,null,null,111],"ISR":[-1,287,null,null,null,null,-18],"ITA":[-1,176,null,null,null,null,-12],"IDN":[-1,155,null,null,null,null,-155],"IRL":[-1,186,null,null,null,null,0],"IRN":[-1,216,null,null,null,null,-18],"IND":[-1,104,null,null,null,null,85],"JAM":[-1,222,null,null,null,null,-25],"JPN":[-1,350,null,null,null,null,4],"KAZ":[-1,309,null,null,null,null,-36],"LBY":[-1,208,null,null,null,null,0],"